00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.280 align:start position:0%
the PlayStation Vita is a remarkable  gaming handheld even two years after its  debut but Sony is beginning to rapidly  phase out the old design in favor of a  refined slimmer Vita in many ways it's  an overall improvement and unlike the  first version it comes bundled with a  free memory card in a free copy of  Borderlands 2 on paper it sounds like a  great value but even though there are  numerous improvements to the hardware  and some free extras sacrifices have  been made along the way and you may find  yourself weighing the benefits of both  models if you're considering picking up  the so called Vita slim the original  Vita is a strong piece of hardware but  it has its share of issues that needed  to be addressed the battery life is  great in standby mode or during gameplay  it typically taps out around the four  hour mark the lackluster battery  performance was also compounded by the  system's proprietary charging port it  negates the viability of common USB  cables and requires a USB port with a  data connection in order to accept a  charge common wall chargers won't cut it  plus it won't charge over USB if the  battery is completely dead it has to be  plugged into a wall socket thankfully  the new Vita resolves some of these  issues you no longer need a special Vita  only cable with the new micro USB port  and you don't need to rely on finicky  port restrictions either plus the  battery in the new Vita is reported to  last longer despite having the same  battery capacity while it's good to see  that the Vita's new screen doesn't  negatively impact battery life it altom  utley has a negative impact on the  overall experience the most notable  difference of the new Vita  is the use of an LCD panel versus the  old Ola D panel used in the original  sure LCD panels are cheaper to produce  which allows Sony to shave off a few  dollars from the Vita price tag but with  the persistent backlight colors look  washed out on the LCD panel compared to  the old version if you've used the  original Vita in any capacity you know  how impressive the O LED display can be  in the moment you look at the new one in  action you instantly recognize that it  fails to produce images that are as  crisp or vibrant if you've never used  the old model the shift in screen  technology won't stand out as much but  you also won't find the display on the  new Vita particularly impressive either  if anything its unremarkable still you  can find improvements in other areas  that make the new Vita an attractive  proposition the new USB port is one but  if you look around you find that the  buttons have also been improved  especially the start select and  PlayStation Home buttons these three  buttons were previously ovoid and sat  flush with the surface making them  unusually difficult to press now they  are represented like any other button  they're circular and raised up making  them far easier to press down especially  when you're trying to take screenshots  by pressing the start and home button at  the same time the new Vita also comes  with one gigabyte of built-in memory  which means that you don't have to have  a memory card in order to store a PSN  account and play games but oddly you  can't use the internal storage and the  included a gigabyte memory card at the  same time finally the new Vita is  slimmer and lighter than the old model  when viewed head-on the two versions  appear to have similar dimensions but  angle the system and you'll notice that  the new model is 20% slimmer it's less  bulky overall and it weighs 15% less in  the original Vita model there's no  getting around the fact that the new  Vita has an inferior screen compared to  its predecessor but it's easy to  appreciate the reduction in size weight  and price plus the changes made to the  USB port and the buttons make it a much  friendlier system to use overall even  though they won't look as good the same  games that worked on the old Vita work  on the new model so at the end of the  day it's worth considering for all of  its advantages
 

